# WebGL: Build Size

WebGL builds are downloaded before every session. Every megabyte of wasm/data is load time and bounce rate. Code contributes through IL2CPP output; packages and assets through data.

## Package discipline

- **No new package dependencies without a size justification.** Every package drags code (IL2CPP), often transitive deps, sometimes streaming assets. State the cost/benefit in the PR when adding one. The Input System package in particular is banned (see the forbidden-apis rule).
- Remove packages that are no longer used; check `Packages/manifest.json` during cleanup passes.
- Prefer writing 200 lines of project code over importing a 2 MB general-purpose library for one function.

## IL2CPP code-size traps

- **Generics explode**: every `SomeGeneric<ValueType>` instantiation generates a full copy of the code. Avoid deeply generic utility layers; prefer concrete types in gameplay code.
- **Reflection defeats stripping** (see no-reflection rule) — reflected code forces IL2CPP to keep everything reachable.
- Keep **Managed Stripping Level: High**. If stripping removes something needed (almost always caused by reflection/serialization), fix the code to reference it statically; `link.xml` entries are a last resort and each one must carry a comment explaining why.

## Asset hygiene (when touching import settings)

- Textures: correct max size + compression per platform; no 4K textures for UI icons.
- Audio: compressed (Vorbis) for music; short SFX can be decompress-on-load; mono where stereo adds nothing.
- Strip unused scenes/resources from build settings; anything under `Resources/` ships whether used or not.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] No new package deps without explicit size justification
- [ ] No new deeply generic layers or reflection that defeats stripping
- [ ] `link.xml` additions are last-resort and commented
